From: meanaverage <18336095+meanaverage@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 09:52:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 03/17] fix(web): dispatch the ready event after clipboard
 initialization

`ready` was dispatched at the end of canvas initialization, before
`ClipboardService.initClipboard()` had run: that awaits a permissions
query, and only then installs the clipboard callbacks. `connect()`
registers those callbacks on the session builder only if they are
installed, so a host that connects as soon as `ready` fires got a
session without a clipboard channel. Connecting after a user action
(as iron-svelte-client does) hides the race.

Dispatch `ready` once the clipboard is initialized (or its
initialization failed), so connecting on it always sets up the
clipboard.

Adds a component test for it. Mounting the component under vitest needs
Svelte's browser build (`resolve.conditions`) and skipping
vite-plugin-svelte's style preprocessing, which fails under vitest 2's
bundled Vite 5; the component's styles are plain CSS.
